---
title: Code of Conduct
description: Official Code of Conduct and Member Regulations for SEDS Sri Lanka and affiliated University Chapters.
---

### 1. Purpose & Core Values

Students for the Exploration and Development of Space Sri Lanka (SEDS Sri Lanka) is dedicated to fostering a professional, safe, collaborative, and inclusive environment for all students, educators, mentors, and space enthusiasts.

Every member, volunteer, and participant in SEDS Sri Lanka activities—including university chapter sessions, national projects, high-altitude balloon launches, hackathons, sky camps, and online forums—is expected to uphold these core principles:

- **Scientific Curiosity & Innovation**: Pushing the frontiers of aerospace, engineering, and astronomy through rigorous inquiry and hands-on experimentation.
- **Mutual Respect & Inclusivity**: Welcoming individuals of all backgrounds, genders, ethnicities, academic fields, and skill levels.
- **Safety First**: Prioritizing human safety and strict operational discipline during all hardware, rocketry, high-voltage, and payload testing.
- **Integrity & Academic Honesty**: Giving credit to contributors, citing research, and maintaining transparent project management.

---

### 2. Expected Behavior

All members of SEDS Sri Lanka agree to:

1. **Collaborate Constructively**: Encourage peers, mentor newcomers, and contribute constructively to team objectives.
2. **Adhere to Safety Protocols**: Follow certified safety checklists before operating tools, electronics, pyrotechnics, chemicals, or launching aerial vehicles.
3. **Respect Club & University Resources**: Use laboratory facilities, maker spaces, equipment, and organizational funds responsibly and solely for approved organizational objectives.
4. **Communicate Professionally**: Maintain professional, respectful language across official communication channels including Discord, GitHub, Slack, and email.
5. **Represent the Organization with Dignity**: Act with professionalism when interacting with academic institutions, international SEDS bodies, sponsors, and the media.

---

### 3. Unacceptable Behavior

The following behaviors are strictly prohibited across all SEDS Sri Lanka spaces, whether physical or digital:

- **Harassment & Discrimination**: Harassment, bullying, hate speech, or discrimination based on race, ethnicity, religion, gender, sexual orientation, disability, or socioeconomic background.
- **Safety Violations**: Willful negligence or unauthorized testing of hazardous materials, propulsion systems, or high-power electronics without certified safety approval and supervision.
- **Academic Misconduct & Plagiarism**: Claiming credit for another student's work, stealing technical designs, or falsifying test/competition data.
- **Misuse of Branding**: Using the official SEDS Sri Lanka name, logo, or domain (`sedssl.org`) for personal commercial gain or unauthorized public statements.
- **Disruption**: Disrupting workshops, lectures, observing nights, or executive committee proceedings.

---

### 4. Enforcement & Reporting

Violations of this Code of Conduct will be reviewed promptly by the SEDS Sri Lanka Executive Committee and relevant Chapter Advisory Boards:

1. **Reporting**: Any member who experiences or witnesses unacceptable behavior should report it to their Chapter Lead or directly to the national Executive Committee at **[contact@sedssl.org](mailto:contact@sedssl.org)**.
2. **Confidentiality**: All reports will be handled confidentially to protect the safety and privacy of the reporting party.
3. **Corrective Action**: Depending on the severity of the violation, actions may range from a private written warning to immediate revocation of membership and expulsion from all national and chapter activities.

---

### 5. Inquiries & Contact

For questions regarding these guidelines, or to seek safety clearance for a student space project:

- **Executive Committee Email**: [contact@sedssl.org](mailto:contact@sedssl.org)
- **Official Domain**: [sedssl.org](https://sedssl.org)
